{%- comment -%}
  ONE FAQ ENTRY as an accessible disclosure.

  Slice 12. Extracted from `faq-list.liquid` because that snippet prints
  entries in two passes (keyed first, then unkeyed — see its ordering
  comment), and two inline copies of this markup would be two places an
  answer could render differently. One renderer, called twice.

  SKIPS AN INCOMPLETE ENTRY. A metaobject saved with a question but no answer
  renders nothing rather than an empty disclosure a customer can open to find
  blank space. The entry stays visible in Admin, so the omission is fixable;
  what it must not do is look like an answer that says nothing.

  ANSWER IS OUTPUT AS THE FIELD TYPE PROVIDES IT. A rich-text metaobject field
  yields safe HTML Shopify itself produced; a multi-line text field yields a
  string that Liquid escapes. Both are correct, and neither is coerced.

  ACCEPTS:
    entry          one faq_entry metaobject (required)
    show_category  true to print the entry's category beneath the answer
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if entry.question != blank and entry.answer != blank -%}
  <details class="carat-faq__item">
    <summary class="carat-faq__question">
      <span class="carat-faq__question-text">{{ entry.question }}</span>
      {{- 'icon-caret.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
    </summary>
    <div class="carat-faq__answer rte">
      {%- comment -%}
        `answer` is a RICH TEXT field. Output bare, Liquid prints its stored
        JSON ({"type":"root",...}) verbatim — a live defect found 2026-10-25
        on /pages/faq. `metafield_tag` renders it as HTML (paragraphs, bold),
        the same filter product-disclosures.liquid uses for rich text.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {{ entry.answer | metafield_tag }}
    </div>
    {%- if show_category and entry.category != blank -%}
      <p class="carat-faq__category">{{ entry.category }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </details>
{%- endif -%}
